    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.base16\n\n### Description\n\nThe `return` keyword in mini.base16 is assigned to `base08`, shouldn't keywords be assigned to `base0E` according to https://github.com/chriskempson/base16/blob/main/styling.md? I have red mapped to `base08`, since `base08` is used for lsp errors. Should errors and the return keyword have the same color?\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNA\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`return` should be mapped to `base08`\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n`return` is mapped to `base0E`.",
